  "body": "ESTATE SALE-- the value could well be in exploring the property's future - whether that means renovating and enhancing the existing home, accommodating extended family, or investigating the redevelopment possibilities that 769sqm (more or less) offers. The choice is yours.\r\n\r\nPositioned  in the tightly held dress circle on Waller Avenue on the Bucklands Beach Peninsula, this 769sqm more or less  level site enjoys a magnificent 180-degree outlook across the water, taking in Rangitoto and beyond. \r\n\r\nEnjoying a northwest-facing aspect capturing all day sunshine and some very spectacular sunsets.\r\n\r\nHeld and cherished by one family for more than 54 years, this much-loved property offers an exceptional combination of space, position, and potential.\r\n\r\nSpread over two levels  the home provides six bedrooms and two to three generous living areas, offering plenty of flexibility for a large family or those considering multigenerational living.\r\n\r\nThe private, established gardens create a peaceful setting, while the expansive outlook provides a constant reminder of just how special this location is.\r\n\r\nZoned for Macleans top schools and exceptionally well positioned for Bucklands Beach Primary and an easy walk to the Intermediate schools and Macleans College, education is totally covered. Sporting facilities, public transport and the ferry service to the CBD and Waiheke Island are all within easy reach.\r\n\r\nThis is a location where lifestyle, position and opportunity come together.\r\n\r\nAfter more than half a century in one family's hands, the time has come for a new chapter.\r\n\r\n* 769sqm more or less prime peninsula land\r\n* 180-degree sea views\r\n* Northwest-facing/glorious sunsets \r\n* Six bedrooms\r\n* A remarkable family history and a future that is yours to shape.\r\n\r\nWe look forward to seeing you at the open homes or if you prefer a private viewing contact Ellen Ming  021450856\r\nellen.ming@raywhite.com",
